CHAPTER V
OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 30
Protection of Women Victims of Violence
The Regional Government is obligated to:
a. guarantee the implementation of the fulfillment of women's rights and the provision of assurance of safety from acts of violence, and efforts of exploitation against women in the region;
b. establish policies, programs, activities for the protection of women and guarantees for victim handling to eliminate all forms of discrimination and acts of violence against women in the region;
c. provide guidance and supervision in efforts to protect women carried out by Regional Apparatus handling the Protection and Empowerment of Women;
d. endeavor to establish women's protection institutions;
e. implement the established policies, programs and activities for the protection of women; and
f. conduct socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of women victims of violence and discrimination;

Article 13
(1) The Regional Government undertakes integrated efforts to prevent violence against women in the Region.
(2) Integrated efforts to prevent violence against women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be coordinated by the Regional Apparatus responsible for the protection and empowerment of women.
(3) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be implemented by:
a. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns that may involve community organizations, universities, professionals as well as customary heads and/or community leaders;
b. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of the rights of women victims of violence;
c. establishing an integrated violence prevention system;
d. providing ease of access to obtain civil rights, education, health, employment, training and funding, welfare improvement and social services;
e. providing education regarding women's rights for the community;
f. fostering and developing community participation and concern for the protection of women from acts of violence;
g. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system; and
h. establishing a cooperation network in efforts to prevent acts of violence with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women.

Article 26
