CHAPTER X
ADMINISTRATIVE SANCTIONS
Article 40
(1) Any person, institution, or entity that deliberately fails to provide protection to women, thereby causing acts of violence against women to occur, allows acts of violence to occur, and/or fails to report to the relevant agency may be subject to administrative sanctions.
(2) Business Entities or non-governmental organizations (NGOs) are obligated to provide Protection to Women and against acts of Violence in their work environment.
(3) Business Entities or non-governmental organizations (NGOs) are obligated to report acts of violence in their work environment to the relevant agency.
(4) Violations as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3) may be subject to administrative sanctions in the form of:
   a. verbal warning;
   b. written warning;
   c. temporary suspension of activities;
   d. termination of cooperation;
   e. revocation of the certificate of registration;
   f. revocation of the operational permit;
   g. sealing;
   h. withdrawal of facilities; and/or
   i. an administrative fine of at least Rp.10,000,000,- (Ten Million Rupiah) and at most Rp.50,000,000,- (Fifty Million Rupiah).
(5) Provisions regarding the procedures for implementing administrative sanctions as referred to in paragraph (4) are regulated in the Regent's Regulation.

